      "type": "h1",
      "text": "ECMAScript 2016"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "New Features in JavaScript 2016"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Supported in all modern browsers since March 2017."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        ["Feature", "Description", ""],
        ["**", "Raises the first operand to the power of the second", ""],
        ["**=", "Raises the value of a variable to the power of the right operand", ""],
        ["Array includes()", "Checks if an element is present in an array", ""]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Browser Support"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "JavaScript 2016 is supported in all modern browsers since March 2017:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": ["", "", "", "", ""],
      "rows": [
        ["Chrome52", "Edge15", "Firefox52", "Safari10.1", "Opera39"],
        ["Jul 2016", "Apr 2017", "Mar 2017", "May 2017", "Aug 2016"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "ES 2016 is not supported in Internet Explorer."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Exponentiation Operator"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "The exponentiation operator (**) raises the first operand to the power of the second operand."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 5;\n\nlet z = x ** 2;",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_es6_exponent1"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "x ** y produces the same result as Math.pow(x, y):"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 5;\n\nlet z = Math.pow(x,2);",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_es6_exponent2"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Exponentiation Assignment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "exponentiation assignment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "**="
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "let x = 5;\n\nx **= 2;",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_es6_exponent3"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "JavaScript Array includes()"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "ECMAScript 2016 introduced Array.includes to arrays."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This allows us to check if an element is present in an array:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "js",
      "text": "const fruits = [\"Banana\", \"Orange\", \"Apple\", \"Mango\"];\n\nfruits.includes(\"Mango\");",
      "caption": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "tryit",
      "url": "https://www.w3schools.com/tryit.asp?filename=tryjs_array_includes"
    }
  ]
}
